# Sensitive Bridge v1.4 Part-Aware Codewords

## Identity

All codeword and part registry reads use canonical `users.username`. Do not query part-aware v1.4 tables by hardware ID.

## Parts

Part numbers are per-client, not global. `part_category` carries the clinical role (`protector`, `exile`, `firefighter`, `manager`, `addict_part`, etc.) and must be preserved in disclosure events.

## Entry Point

After Phase C, `NateCheckInAgent.detect_codeword_disclosure(message, username)` is the canonical listener. It returns matched codeword ID, disclosure type, part name/number/category, and addiction link. Existing `check_codeword` is fallback only.

## Clinical Boundary

Codeword matching may elevate acuity silently, but it must not expose the codeword, part name, or addiction link to the client response.
